z3p = z3b with every mid-game formation switch off: CASH_KINGS 0 (no rescue formation at any king count), RICH_FIX
false, RICH_LATE 0, RICH_MORE 0, RICH_GAP 0. What is left is z1z + tools/ledger.py + CASH_END 1880: from r1880 a lone
king's babies run CASH's formation for a second king, no raw needed, while the bank keeps the new king alive to r2000
(Baby.cashEnd). Kings alive at r2000 weigh 0.5 of war points (2-1 is 33-17).
Replica evidence on z1z's set-3 block 1: z2x (the full bundle) and z3b (z2x minus the two-king CASH and one-king
RICH_FIX) both gained corridorofdoomanddespair B vs Varun, where CASH_END formed a second king at r1906 and won at
r2000 (z1z lost on points). Their losses were mid-game formations that starved the bank: rose A (CASH/RICH_MORE at
r970/r981) and minimaze A (one-king RICH_FIX at r825). z3p keeps only the endgame king.

Falsifiers, registered before any z3p game:
1. Local exactness: games where no lone king reaches r1880 must replay z1z's game (replay_eq vs ~/diag26b/cy's z1z
   dumps, 16 games that end before r500).
2. Local endgame games vs araid where z1z is a lone king at r1880: the second king must form by r1960 and live to
   r2000, and no z1z win may turn into a loss.
3. Replica: block rules (TRAINING_ALGORITHM s4) against z1z's set-3 block 17946-17961. On block 1 every cell but
   corridorofdoomanddespair B should replay z1z's game; that cell should stay a win.
